DS3D multi-sensor mixer is an implementation of `ds3d::datamixer` which combines
several input streams into one `ds3d::datamap`. It matches the frames arriving
from multiple cameras and LiDARs on their timestamps and emits a single
synchronized datamap per fused frame, which is what a sensor-fusion inference
filter expects on its input.

Unlike the other DS3D modules this one does depend on GStreamer, because it
handles DeepStream video buffers and batch metadata on its video input pads.

`libnvds_3d_multisensor_mixer.so` is built from these source files. and the
mixer is created through API `createMultiSensorMixer`. Application users can
call this API to instantiate this datamixer.

The config content shall as:

    type: ds3d::datamixer
    out_caps: ds3d/datamap
    custom_lib_path: libnvds_3d_multisensor_mixer.so
    custom_create_function: createMultiSensorMixer
    config_body:
       ...

Any custom `ds3d::datamixer` must derive from `ds3d::BaseImplDataMixer` for data mixing
And implement the following interfaces:

    ErrCode startImpl(const std::string& content, const std::string& path) override;
    ErrCode processImpl(
        const int portId, GuardDataMap datamap,
        OnGuardDataCBImpl inputConsumedCb) override;
    ErrCode setOutputCbImpl(OnGuardDataCBImpl outputDataCb) override;
    ErrCode updateInputImpl(int portId, MixerUpdate updateType) override;
    ErrCode stopImpl() override;
    ErrCode flushImpl() override;

In addition, users also need export a C-API for application to intiate this datamixer.
The exported C-API name is not limited. In this sample, it is `createMultiSensorMixer`.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://docs.nvidia.com/metropolis/deepstream/dev-guide/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual.html

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_3d_common.so (build and install ds3d/common first)
- libgstreamer1.0 Development package
- libyaml-cpp Development package
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this `ds3d::datamixer` lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
- Verify `libnvds_3d_multisensor_mixer.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
